.local/
.agent/
.claude.json

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials & runtime state
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
credentials.json
token.json
gmail-sync-log.json
sync-log.json

# Build artifacts
deno.lock
docs/walkthroughs/*/public/
docs/assets/agent-memory/promotional/generated-backgrounds/**/result.json
docs/assets/agent-memory/screenshots/**/.chrome-*/
integrations/openclaw-agent-memory/dist/

# Evaluation corpora built from real data — Linear issues, exported notes, anything
# pointed at by OB1_EVAL_CORPUS. The harnesses default to /tmp for this reason, but
# it is an easy convenience to drop one in the repo and this is a PUBLIC repository.
# The synthetic corpus (evals/corpus.ts) is committed deliberately; these are not.
*-corpus.json
evals/corpus-*.json
evals/*.local.json

# Recipe run output — full email and memory text, never to be committed.
# gmail-smart-pull writes its packs and its Gmail state under
# recipes/gmail-smart-pull/data/ (the OAuth token lives beside the script, in
# its own ignored file); the atomizer reads and writes data/atomic-memories/
# relative to the CURRENT DIRECTORY, so from the repo root that is
# /data/atomic-memories/. scripts/check-fork-consistency.mjs skips ignored
# files, so a pulled email that happens to contain a flagged string cannot fail
# the shell-hazard check on the machine that pulled it.
recipes/*/data/
/data/atomic-memories/
